            <div xml:id="d892">

                <pb facs="0940" n="842" sameAs="frus:frus1920v01/pg842"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">818.6363Am6/49: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at San José</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Chase</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >San José</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-08-30T11:00:00-05:36"><hi rendition="#italic">August 30,
                                1920—11 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received August 31—5:07
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>59. President Acosta vetoed all acts of the final session of Congress including
                    the resolution referred to in my telegram of July 19, 6 p.m., Sinclair oil
                    concession, which had passed Congress that day over a former voting [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">veto?</hi>], and much other important legislation,
                    alleging that regular term expired a day earlier by limitation of time.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Chase</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
